               of cardiac defects associated with TBX5 mutations in humans
               suggests multiple roles for the transcription factor in cardiac
               development and function. Animal models demonstrate similar
               defects and have provided a useful platform for investigating the
               roles of TBX5 during embryonic development. During early cardiac
               development, TBX5 appears to act primarily as a transcriptional
               activator of genes associated with cardiomyocyte maturation and
