                  appears both as sub- or metacentric that is the same size as
                  small chromosomes of standard complement. Both karyotypically
                  stable and unstable species possess Bs. The presence of Bs in
                  certain species influences the cell division, the degree of
                  recombination, the development, a number of quantitative
                  characteristics, the host-parasite interactions and their
                  behaviour. There is at least some data on molecular structure
                  of Bs recorded in nearly a quarter of species. Nevertheless, a
                  more detailed molecular composition of Bs presently known for
