  doi          = {10.1038/378789a0},
  abstract     = {In Western Europe and the United States approximately 1 in 12
                  women develop breast cancer. A small proportion of breast
                  cancer cases, in particular those arising at a young age, are
                  attributable to a highly penetrant, autosomal dominant
                  predisposition to the disease. The breast cancer
