  abstract     = {T cells play critical roles in immune responses to pathogens,
                  autoimmunity, and antitumor immunity. During the past few
                  decades, increasing numbers of studies have demonstrated the
                  significance of protein ubiquitination in T cell-mediated
                  immunity. Several E3 ubiquitin ligases and deubiquitinases
                  (DUBs) have been identified as either positive or negative
                  regulators of T cell development and function. In this review,
                  we mainly focus on the roles of DUBs (especially
                  ubiquitin-specific proteases (USPs)) in modulating T cell
