                  fibroblasts. This feature could not account for either
                  increased DNA repair activity or higher efficacy of the
                  antioxygenic system and pointed, instead, to an intrinsic
                  nuclear stability which might be typical of centenarian
                  fibroblasts and potentially functional to longevity.},
  urldate      = {2025-10-09},
