  date         = {2022-04},
  doi          = {10.1038/s41586-022-04618-z},
  abstract     = {The rates and patterns of somatic mutation in normal tissues
                  are largely unknown outside of humans1-7. Comparative analyses
                  can shed light on the diversity of mutagenesis across species,
                  and on long-standing hypotheses about the evolution of somatic
                  mutation rates and their role in cancer and ageing. Here we
                  performed whole-genome sequencing of 208 intestinal crypts
                  from 56 individuals to study the landscape of somatic mutation
                  across 16 mammalian species. We found that somatic mutagenesis
                  was dominated by seemingly endogenous mutational processes in
