  abstract     = {Forkhead box (FOX) family transcription factors play essential
                  roles in development, tissue homeostasis, and disease.
                  Although the biology of several FOX proteins has been studied
                  in depth, it is unclear to what extent these findings apply to
                  even closely related family members, which frequently exert
                  overlapping but non-redundant functions. To help address this
                  question, we have generated a uniform, ready-to-use expression
                  library of all 44 human FOX transcription factors with a
                  convenient peptide tag for parallel screening assays. In
