  abstract     = {The value of a continuous character evolving on a phylogenetic
                  tree is commonly modelled as the location of a particle moving
                  under one-dimensional Brownian motion with constant rate. The
                  Brownian motion model is best suited to characters evolving
                  under neutral drift or tracking an optimum that drifts
