                  datasets identified an unexpected risk factor for CVD,
                  somatically acquired DNA mutations. In this review, we provide
                  an overview of somatic mutations and their contributions to
                  CVD. We focus on the most common and well described
                  manifestation, clonal hematopoiesis of indeterminate potential
                  (CHIP). We also review the currently available data regarding
