                  reproductive rate and is not influenced by diet, colony size
                  or the source of the record. These results are largely
                  consistent with extrinsic mortality risk acting as a
                  determinant of bat longevity. Nevertheless, the strong
                  association between life span and both reproductive rate and
                  hibernation also suggests that bat longevity is strongly
                  influenced by seasonal allocation of non-renewable resources
                  to reproduction. We speculate that hibernation may provide a
