  doi          = {10.1111/acel.12283},
  abstract     = {Mammals differ more than 100-fold in maximum lifespan, which
                  can be altered in either direction during evolution, but the
                  molecular basis for natural changes in longevity is not
                  understood. Divergent evolution of mammals also led to
                  extensive changes in gene expression within and between
                  lineages. To understand the relationship between lifespan and
                  variation in gene expression, we carried out RNA-seq-based
                  gene expression analyses of liver, kidney, and brain of 33
